{"resourceIdentifier":"3566","resourceName":"Livelihood improvement by agroforestry plantation in India","description":"Adopting an agroforestry approach would be a practical alternative to meet the growing demand for wood and other tree-based products because it is a system that can offer both food and wood while also preserving and rehabilitating the ecosystem. The proposed ARR VCS project aims to support small-scale farmers in Nasik, Ahmednagar districts in India, using sustainable plantations in order to give them financial advantages and assure GHG mitigation over the period of its lifetime. The total project area of expected to be covered in the project is 4000 hectares.","location":{"latitude":19.997451,"longitude":73.789799},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-08-15","endExclusive":"2022-09-15","endInclusive":"2022-09-14"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3566"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Maharashtra"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"6420"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4000 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Carbon Check (India) Private Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"17/04/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 11/06/2018 - 10/06/2048"}]}]}],"document